hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22264","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Said ibn Jumhan narrated to us, and Abd al-Samad narrated to me Said ibn Jumhan, from Safina, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The caliphate is thirty years, then after that there will be kingship. Safina said: Count the caliphate of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, two years, and the caliphate of Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, ten years, and the caliphate of Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, twelve years, and the caliphate of Ali, six years, may Allah be pleased with them."
"22265","Waki narrated to us, from Ali, meaning Ibn Mubarak, from Yahya, from Safina, that a man pierced his she-camel with a palm trunk, so he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he ordered them to eat it."
"22266","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Said ibn Jumhan, from Safina, that he used to carry many things, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: You are Safina."
"22267","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, from Said ibn Jumhan, he said: I heard Safina narrating that a man guested Ali ibn Abi Talib, and they made food for him. Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, said: Had we called the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he ate with us. They sent to him, and he came and took the two doorposts, and a curtain had been hung in a corner of the house. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw it, he returned. Fatima said to Ali: Follow him and say to him: What made you return? He followed him and said: What made you return, O Messenger of Allah? He said: It is not for me, or: It is not for a prophet to enter a decorated house."
"22268","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to me, from Said ibn Jumhan, Safina Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The caliphate is thirty years, then kingship, and he mentioned it."
"22269","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Imran al-Nakhli, from a freedman of Umm Salama, he said: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a journey, and we ended at a valley. He said: So I began carrying the people across or carrying them. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: You were today nothing but Safina, or: You are nothing but Safina. It was said to Sharik: He is Safina, the freedman of Umm Salama, may Allah be pleased with her."
"22270","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us, Said ibn Jumhan informed us, from Safina, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a journey, and whenever some of the people tired, he cast upon me his sword, his shield, and his spear, until I carried much of that. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You are Safina."
"22271","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Said ibn Jumhan narrated to us, Safina Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us that a man guested Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and he made food for him. Fatima said: Had we called the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He mentioned the like of the hadith of Abu Kamil. They called him, and he came and placed his hand upon the two doorposts, and saw a curtain in a corner of the house, and returned. Fatima said to Ali: Catch him and say to him: Why did you return, O Messenger of Allah? He said: It is not for me to enter a decorated house."
"22272","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Said ibn Jumhan narrated to us, from Safina Abi Abd al-Rahman, he said: Umm Salama freed me and stipulated upon me that I serve the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as long as he lives."
"22273","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Hashraj Ibn Nubata al-Absi, a Kufan, narrated to us, Said ibn Jumhan narrated to us, Safina narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The caliphate in my nation is thirty years, then kingship after that. Then Safina said to me: Count the caliphate of Abu Bakr, and the caliphate of Umar, and the caliphate of Uthman, and count the caliphate of Ali, may Allah, the Exalted, be pleased with them. He said: So we found it thirty years. Then I looked after that at the caliphs and did not find thirty agreeing for them."
"22274","So I said to Said: Where did you meet Safina? He said: I met him at Batn Nakhl in the time of al-Hajjaj, and I stayed with him eight nights asking him about the hadiths of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: I said to him: What is your name? He said: I will not inform you; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, named me Safina. I said: And why did he name you Safina? He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out with his companions, and their baggage became heavy upon them, so he said to me: Spread your cloak. I spread it, and they placed their baggage in it, then they carried it upon me. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Carry, for you are only Safina. Had I carried that day the load of a camel, or two camels, or three, or four, or five, or six, or seven, it would not have been heavy upon me, except that they become harsh."
"22275","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Hashraj narrated to us, Said ibn Jumhan narrated to me, from Safina, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us and said: Verily there was no prophet before me except he warned his nation of the Dajjal. He is blind in his left eye, in his right eye is a thick film, written between his eyes is disbeliever. He comes out with two valleys, one of them a garden and the other fire; his fire is a garden and his garden is fire. With him are two angels from the angels resembling two prophets from the prophets; had I wished I would have named them with their names and the names of their fathers. One of them is on his right and the other on his left, and that is a trial. The Dajjal says: Am I not your Lord? Do I not give life and cause death? One of the two angels says to him: You have lied; none of the people hears him except his companion. He says to him: You have told the truth, and the people hear him and think he is only confirming the Dajjal, and that is a trial. Then he proceeds until he comes to Madina, and he is not permitted therein, and he says: This is the village of that man. Then he proceeds until he comes to Sham, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, destroys him at Aqabat Afiq."
"22276","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Abu Rayhana narrated to me, my father said, and Ali named him Abd Allah ibn Matar, he said: Safina, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sufficed by the mudd for wudu, and the sa washed him from janaba."
"22277","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Rayhana narrated to us, from Safina, the companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to bathe with the sa and purify himself with the mudd."
"22278","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Said ibn Jumhan, from Safina, he said: We were in a journey. He said: Whenever a man tired, he cast upon me his clothes, a shield or a sword, until I carried much of that. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You are Safina."
"22279","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Said ibn Jumhan informed us, Safina narrated to me that a man guested Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and he made food for him. Fatima said to Ali: Had you called the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he ate with us. We called him, and he came and took the two doorposts, and we had hung a curtain in a corner of the house. When he saw it, he returned. Fatima said to Ali: Catch him and see what made him return. He said: What turned you back, O Prophet of Allah? He said: It is not for a prophet to enter a decorated house."
